{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>Only by lot shall the land be divided.</b> The matter of the lot was because of the good portion and the bad portion: whoever's lot came up a good portion, he had it; and whoever's lot came up a bad portion, they would compensate him with money; and whoever had a good portion would pay money to the one whose hand held a bad portion." "<b>And behold,</b> the division of the land was in this order: Elazar was vested in the Urim and Tummim, and all Israel stood before him, and the urns of the tribes and the urns of the territories were set before him. And he would direct his mind by means of the Holy Spirit (ru'aḥ ha-kodesh) and say: 'If Zevulun comes up, the territory of Akko comes up with it.' He would shake the urn of the tribes and Zevulun came up in his hand; he would shake the urn of the territories and the territory of Akko came up in his hand. And he would again direct his mind by means of the Holy Spirit (ru'aḥ ha-kodesh) and say: 'If Naftali comes up, the territory of Ginossar comes up with it.' He would shake the urn of the tribes and Naftali came up in his hand; he would shake the urn of the territories and the territory of Ginossar came up — and so for every tribe. And the tribe would divide its portion among the father's houses according to those who went out of Egypt: the tribe that had many father's houses at their going out of Egypt received many portions, even though they are now few, as it says: <b>to the names of the tribes of their fathers</b> they shall inherit — these are those who went out of Egypt — and to exclude the converts."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:17.776864734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}